WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:09.360
So Donald Trump has been freaking out on Twitter,&nbsp;
melting down since last night, highly triggered by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:09.360 --> 00:00:18.320
the Senate results, and Trump again raising this&nbsp;
idea of huge dumps of votes. The guy can't behave&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:18.320 --> 00:00:24.080
normally for five minutes. And Donald Trump&nbsp;
even in advance of last night's results,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:24.080 --> 00:00:29.280
which we actually knew relatively quickly,&nbsp;
all things considered, tweeting around 10:00&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:29.280 --> 00:00:37.120
p.m. last night, looks like they are setting up a&nbsp;
big voter dump against the Republican candidates&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:37.120 --> 00:00:43.040
waiting to see how many votes they need. And&nbsp;
of course, this never happened. Donald Trump,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:43.040 --> 00:00:47.680
whatever massive dumps he was involved in or&nbsp;
believed were coming, it just never happened from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:47.680 --> 00:00:53.200
the standpoint of the race. And in fact, Democrats&nbsp;
were winning. Early Trump scenario is always&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:53.200 --> 00:00:58.720
Republicans are way ahead and then massive dumps&nbsp;
come in. And then Democrats when Democrats were&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:58.720 --> 00:01:03.600
winning early and then the race has tightened&nbsp;
as more votes were counted. And then it was just&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:03.600 --> 00:01:09.200
slow, slow, slow, steady vote counts going one&nbsp;
way and the other. And eventually it became clear&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:09.200 --> 00:01:14.160
that Democrats would win by a small margin&nbsp;
in both races because outstanding votes were&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:14.160 --> 00:01:21.760
overwhelmingly from very, very blue areas, areas,&nbsp;
areas that went three to two for the Democratic&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:21.760 --> 00:01:28.640
challengers, even even three to one in some&nbsp;
cases. So no massive dumps, no small dumps,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:28.640 --> 00:01:34.640
just an election that was counted. And and it was&nbsp;
all pretty unremarkable from the standpoint of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:34.640 --> 00:01:41.280
election integrity and counting. And it really set&nbsp;
Trump off. And he spent most of the night tweeting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:41.280 --> 00:01:46.080
and retweeting stuff, tweeting at midnight&nbsp;
Eastern and then at 1:00 a.m., calling on Mike&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:46.080 --> 00:01:52.160
Pence to steal him the presidency saying, quote,&nbsp;
If Vice President Mike Pence comes through for us,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:52.800 --> 00:01:58.400
we will win the presidency. Many states want to&nbsp;
decertify the mistake they made in certifying&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:58.400 --> 00:02:04.560
incorrect and even fraudulent numbers in a&nbsp;
process not approved by their state legislatures,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:04.560 --> 00:02:11.120
which it must be. Those are all lies, by the way.&nbsp;
And Trump adds, Mitt can send it back. That won't&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:11.120 --> 00:02:16.720
happen. Mike Pence reportedly explaining to Trump&nbsp;
yesterday, I can't overturn the results. And we'll&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:16.720 --> 00:02:21.920
talk a little bit about that later based on a&nbsp;
very good New York Times report. But finishing up&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:21.920 --> 00:02:27.920
with the Trump meltdown. Then this morning, again,&nbsp;
Donald Trump just out of control, first attacking&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:27.920 --> 00:02:36.320
reporter Chuck Todd as Sleepy Eyes. Chuck Todd is&nbsp;
so happy with the fake voter tabulation process&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:36.320 --> 00:02:42.720
that he can't even get the words out straight.&nbsp;
Sad to watch. And Trump's anger knows no limits.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:42.720 --> 00:02:48.880
He will attack anybody for anything at any time&nbsp;
when he's melting down again, claiming, quote,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:48.880 --> 00:02:55.360
states want to correct their votes, which they now&nbsp;
know were based on irregularity, irregularities&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:55.360 --> 00:03:02.720
and fraud, plus corrupt process, never received&nbsp;
legislative approval. All Mike Pence has to do is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:02.720 --> 00:03:10.000
send them back to the states and we win. Do it,&nbsp;
Mike. This is a time for extreme courage. And&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:10.000 --> 00:03:15.360
behind the scenes, there are reports that Trump&nbsp;
is reportedly going to absolutely turn on his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:15.360 --> 00:03:20.800
own. Vice President Mike Pence. If Pence doesn't&nbsp;
do something today, when the vote count starts,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:21.440 --> 00:03:26.240
which we will be covering live, and then&nbsp;
apparently realizing that the Senate is lost.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:26.240 --> 00:03:33.040
Donald Trump sending out an all caps tweet this&nbsp;
morning saying the Republican Party and more&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:33.040 --> 00:03:41.760
importantly, our country needs the presidency more&nbsp;
than ever before. The power of the veto suggesting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:41.760 --> 00:03:47.120
Democrats will have the House, Democrats will&nbsp;
have the Senate. You need me there to veto the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:47.120 --> 00:03:54.880
things that they will do. Truly crumbling before&nbsp;
our very eyes, the Republican Party collapsing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:54.880 --> 00:04:01.200
around Donald Trump. And we we essentially have&nbsp;
to see what else he breaks on the way out. Whoa,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:01.200 --> 00:04:05.520
my microphone. They're flipping out there. We have&nbsp;
to see what else he breaks on the way out. As I've&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:05.520 --> 00:04:10.960
